// Editor-only. No CI job lints markdown; this exists so a stock
// markdownlint setup does not flag the repo's own conventions.
{
  // MD041 — "first line in a file should be a top-level heading" — is
  // off repo-wide. The driver is changelogs: 22 of the 24 package
  // CHANGELOG.md files open at `## <version>`, the format
  // `flutter create` generates and the one pub.dev parses as a version
  // heading. The rule is wrong for those files rather than the reverse,
  // and markdownlint cannot scope a rule to a filename glob.
  //
  // It also fires on PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md (opens at `## What`) and
  // on the package READMEs still carrying the pub template, which open
  // with the template's HTML comment. Those READMEs are a real gap —
  // tracked separately, see #198 — not something a lint rule should be
  // left on to nag about.
  "MD041": false
}
